+## 6. Addendum, written after the push was rejected — TWO RUNS EXECUTED THIS DAY
+
+This log was written by the **desktop** run. When the founder ran its push block it was
+rejected: the origin had moved. The **cloud** run had executed at **09:32 UTC** — roughly
+five and a half hours after its `0 4 * * *` cron — and had done a complete five-function day
+against the same parent commit. Two runs, one date, seven files touched by both, and **both
+filed a ruling numbered #51**.
+
+**The cloud run's day is the record, and on content it was the better day.** Its pair verdict
+returned **four** notes to this run's one. One of the three it found alone —
+*the crowned improver's own floor was missing*, a standing prohibition of that very
+commission — **this run checked and passed.** That is worth stating plainly rather than
+softening: the desktop verdict was not wrong, it was less thorough, and it is superseded.
+
+**What survived from this run, and why it could not have come from the cloud.** The stale
+`web/dist` is a working-tree artefact of the founder's machine. **CI checks out clean, so
+there is no forty-eight-day-old build for `qa_jsonld` to find there** — the input defect was
+structurally invisible to the cloud run and would have remained so indefinitely. Likewise the
+workflow wiring: the cloud identity is refused write access to `.github/workflows/**`, so
+`qa_dist_input` could only be gated as a build step from a desktop session.
+
+**The convergence is the day's strongest single finding.** Both runs, independently and
+without sight of each other, returned the unnamed Principal Investigator. The cloud run
+additionally found **Hilaire Hounkpodoté** in the same condition — named in `sources[]` in
+both languages, reduced in both bodies to a periphrasis. Two readers, one piece, the same
+class, twice. Ruling **#53** carries it; the desktop's two rulings renumber to **#52** and
+**#53**, the cloud's keeps **#51**.
+
+**Reconciliation, as executed:** `main` reset to the cloud's `2d9d13f`; the desktop commit
+parked on branch `desktop-2026-09-15`, nothing lost. The article pair keeps the **cloud's**
+edits. This log and the desktop brief are retained under a `-desktop` suffix. **The desktop
+verdict file was dropped rather than archived** — two verdict files for one pair is a hazard
+to the Verifier's next run, and the cloud's strictly contains it.
+
+### `qa_render` cannot run in this sandbox, and says so
+
+The cloud's new assertion needs headless Chrome. This sandbox has none, and `qa_render`
+**exits 1 rather than skipping** — correct, by its own design and by the 09-13 rule. The
+operational consequence, recorded because it is now permanent: **a desktop session can no
+longer run the full gate set**, since `npm run build` invokes `qa_render` at `postbuild`.
+The CI runner has Chrome, so the deploy gate is unaffected. Verified on the merged tree:
+build exit 0 at 120 pages, and **15 of 16 assertions PASS**, the sixteenth being `qa_render`
+failing loudly on a missing browser rather than passing quietly on nothing.
+
+### Cadence, decided the same evening
+
+The founder's call: **the cloud is the operation; the desktop schedules are disabled.** Both
+were paused. The cron moved off the contended `:00` minute — daily `0 4` → `23 4`, weekly
+`0 5` → `23 5` — with the reason written into the workflow file at the point of change. If a
+run is still hours late on the new offset, the delay is not contention, and the next step is
+to stop planning the day around the cron at all.
+
+— Manager · written 2026-09-15, appended after the collision was found
